{"text": "March 3, 2020 - Polling Place Locations\n\nYou can return your voted ballot to any of the polling locations listed below on Election Day, March 3, from 7am to 8pm\nor you can use one of the following options to return your ballot no later than 8pm Election Day.\n\ne = Mail it in the return envelope provided. Mail your vote-by-mail ballot the week before Election Day. The earlier\nthe better! Ballots must be postmarked no later than March 3 and received by March 6.\n\ne Hand deliver it to the County Clerk/Elections Department or the City Clerks\u2019 offices in Capitola, Santa Cruz,\nScotts Valley, or Watsonville during regular business hours.\n\ne 24-hour drop boxes are located throughout the County at:\no 701 Ocean St, Santa Cruz, in front of the county \u00a9 316 Rodriguez St, Watsonville public lot 14\n\nbuilding\n\nfe)\n\nUC Santa Cruz - Quarry Plaza\n\n\u00a9 212 Church St, Santa Cruz, public parking lot o Graham Hill & Mt. Hermon Rd., Felton Covered\n\no 1 Civic Ctr. Dr, Scotts Valley City Hall parking lot\n\nBridge Park parking lot\n\no 420 Capitola Ave, Capitola City Hall parking lot o Cabrillo College parking lot R\nFor additional drop box locations go online to www.votescount.com\n\ne Weekend hours on February 29 and March 1 from 9am to 5pm at 10 locations throughout Santa Cruz County.\nVisit the County Clerk/Elections Department\u2019s website www.votescount.com for locations.\n\n) 831-454-2060 * 866-282-5900 (toll-free) * TDD: 711 * info@votescount.com\n\nAptos\n\nChrist Lutheran Church\n10707 Soquel Dr (20101)\n\nValencia Hall\n2555 Valencia Rd (20150, 20551)\n\nSanta Cruz Baptist Church\n(Formerly First Baptist Church)\n7565 Sunset Way (20232)\n\nAegis of Aptos Assisted Living\n125 Heather Terrace (20242, 20280\n\nEpiscopal Church of St. John\n125 Canterbury Dr (20260, 20300)\n\nTemple Beth El Jewish Comm. Center\n3055 Porter Gulch Rd (20221)\n\nAptos United Methodist Church\n(Formerly Community Methodist Church)\n221 Thunderbird Dr (20520, 2